'''''Doodia caudata''''' is a [[species]] of dimorphic, evergreen [[fern]] in the family [[Blechnaceae]], native to [[Australia]] and [[New Zealand]]. Upright clusters of fertile fronds reach {{cvt|25|cm|0}} in length. It has been introduced to the [[Azores]], [[Madeira]] and [[Sri Lanka]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Doodia caudata (Cav.) R. Br. |url=https://www.catalogueoflife.org/data/taxon/6DG3V |publisher=[[Catalogue of Life]] |access-date=11 August 2022}}</ref>

